The JMAP state-delta test flags this message and moves it between JmapState and
JmapStateArchive.

APPENDed into its own mailbox rather than COPYed from INBOX, and that distinction is the
point: JMAP models a message in several mailboxes as ONE Email with several mailboxIds, so
an IMAP COPY inside one account does not mint a second object — it adds a mailbox to the
existing one. A test that then MOVEd "its copy" would be replacing the mailboxIds of the
shared baseline, dragging it out of INBOX and Archive and breaking every count asserted
there. This message belongs to nothing else, so moving it disturbs nothing else.
